  ],
  "text": "Bring a deep sea fish to the surface and it does not explode. It melts. Squeeze anything hard enough and it fails. That is the intuition we start with. But a deep sea body has nothing inside it that can be crushed. No air pockets. No swim bladder. Nothing hollow anywhere. The body is mostly water, at exactly the pressure of the water outside it. Which means the danger was never going down. It is coming up. That famous ugly blobfish photograph is just a fish that has been decompressed. It was never ugly. It was perfectly fine until we dragged it into our world. One of these every day. Follow so you do not miss tomorrow.",
  "voice": "802e3bc2b27e49c2995d23ef70e6ac89",
  "model": "s2.1-pro-free"
